<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 12.17 pct, M2 up 3.5 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 12.17 pct, M2 up 3.5 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 693.8 billion levs on May 9 from 618.5 billion levs a week earlier and M2 edged up to 3,228.2 billion levs from 3,119 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 3.03 percent to 3,398.5 billion levs in the week to May 9.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixings of 1,499.4 levs per dollar for May 9, 1,492.8 for May 2 and 1,467.8 for April 25.</p>
